{"seq":3,"slug":"english-grammar-advanced","title":"英语语法进阶","stage":"DONE","category":"english-learning","chapterCount":6,"docCount":24,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced","rating":{"composite":3.75,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.2,"coverage":3.75,"positioning":4,"strategic":3},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.42,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":3.25}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"英语语法进阶-简介\">英语语法进阶 简介</h1><p>英语语法的基础规则大多数学习者在中学阶段就已掌握，但从&quot;知道规则&quot;到&quot;自如运用&quot;之间存在一道巨大的鸿沟。许多有多年英语经验的人仍然会在时态一致性、虚拟语气和从句嵌套上犯错，原因不在于他们不够努力，而在于他们从未系统地梳理过中高级语法的内在逻辑。英语语法进阶正是为了填补这一空白——它不重复基础规则，而是聚焦那些决定表达精确度和文体品质的高阶语法现象。</p>\n<p>本知识库面向已具备中级英语水平的学习者，尤其适合需要用英语进行学术写作、技术文档撰写或专业沟通的程序员和知识工作者。如果你能读懂英文技术文章但写作时总觉得句式单调，或者阅读复杂长句时偶尔迷失在从句层级中，那么这里的内容将帮助你突破瓶颈。</p>\n<p>全书共分六个章节：</p>\n<p>第一章<strong>复杂时态与体</strong>深入剖析英语时态系统中最容易混淆的部分，包括完成时的对比、将来时与进行体的交互、时态一致性原则以及转述语中的时态回退规则。</p>\n<p>第二章<strong>条件句与虚拟语气</strong>系统讲解条件句的四种基本类型及其混合形式，探讨虚拟语气在正式语境中的多种用法，并深入分析 wish 和 if only 引导的非真实愿望表达。</p>\n<p>第三章<strong>从句精通</strong>全面覆盖关系从句、名词从句和状语从句的高级用法，特别关注从句的简化形式——分词短语和独立主格结构，帮助你在保持清晰的前提下提升句子密度。</p>\n<p>第四章<strong>特殊句式</strong>介绍倒装、强调与分裂句、省略与替代以及平行结构这四种打破常规语序的修辞手段，让你的表达从&quot;正确&quot;迈向&quot;有力&quot;。</p>\n<p>第五章<strong>动词模式</strong>聚焦动词后接结构的复杂性，从动名词与不定式的语义差异到短语动词的构成规律，再到使役结构和转述动词的搭配模式，帮你建立动词运用的完整心智模型。</p>\n<p>第六章<strong>连贯与风格</strong>从语法准确性上升到篇章质量，探讨句式多样性、学术缓和语、标点精通和语域正式度四个维度，让你的写作不仅无错，而且有风格。</p>\n<p>建议按章节顺序阅读。前三章夯实时态、虚拟语气和从句这三大语法支柱，第四章和第五章拓展句式表达的广度与深度，第六章将所有语法能力整合为连贯、得体的写作风格。如果你有明确的薄弱环节，也可以直接跳到对应章节重点突破。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"complex-tenses-aspect","title":"复杂时态与体","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/complex-tenses-aspect","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"present-perfect-vs-past-perfect","title":"现在完成时与过去完成时","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/complex-tenses-aspect/present-perfect-vs-past-perfect"},{"seq":2,"slug":"future-and-progressive-aspect","title":"将来时与进行体","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/complex-tenses-aspect/future-and-progressive-aspect"},{"seq":3,"slug":"tense-consistency","title":"时态一致性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/complex-tenses-aspect/tense-consistency"},{"seq":4,"slug":"tense-in-reported-speech","title":"转述语中的时态","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/complex-tenses-aspect/tense-in-reported-speech"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"conditional-subjunctive","title":"条件句与虚拟语气","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/conditional-subjunctive","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"conditional-types","title":"条件句类型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/conditional-subjunctive/conditional-types"},{"seq":2,"slug":"mixed-conditionals","title":"混合条件句","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/conditional-subjunctive/mixed-conditionals"},{"seq":3,"slug":"subjunctive-mood","title":"虚拟语气","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/conditional-subjunctive/subjunctive-mood"},{"seq":4,"slug":"wish-and-if-only","title":"Wish 与 If Only 句型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/conditional-subjunctive/wish-and-if-only"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"clause-mastery","title":"从句精通","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/clause-mastery","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"relative-clauses","title":"关系从句","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/clause-mastery/relative-clauses"},{"seq":2,"slug":"noun-clauses","title":"名词性从句","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/clause-mastery/noun-clauses"},{"seq":3,"slug":"adverbial-clauses","title":"状语从句","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/clause-mastery/adverbial-clauses"},{"seq":4,"slug":"reduced-clauses","title":"从句简化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/clause-mastery/reduced-clauses"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"special-structures","title":"特殊句式","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/special-structures","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"inversion","title":"倒装句","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/special-structures/inversion"},{"seq":2,"slug":"emphatic-and-cleft","title":"强调句与分裂句","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/special-structures/emphatic-and-cleft"},{"seq":3,"slug":"ellipsis-and-substitution","title":"省略与替代","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/special-structures/ellipsis-and-substitution"},{"seq":4,"slug":"parallel-structure","title":"平行结构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/special-structures/parallel-structure"}]},{"seq":5,"slug":"verb-patterns","title":"动词模式","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/verb-patterns","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"gerund-vs-infinitive","title":"动名词与不定式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/verb-patterns/gerund-vs-infinitive"},{"seq":2,"slug":"phrasal-verbs","title":"短语动词","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/verb-patterns/phrasal-verbs"},{"seq":3,"slug":"causative-structures","title":"使役结构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/verb-patterns/causative-structures"},{"seq":4,"slug":"reporting-verbs","title":"转述动词","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/verb-patterns/reporting-verbs"}]},{"seq":6,"slug":"coherence-and-style","title":"连贯与风格","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/coherence-and-style","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"sentence-variety","title":"句式多样性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/coherence-and-style/sentence-variety"},{"seq":2,"slug":"academic-hedging","title":"学术对冲表达","url":"/l-doc-books/h/english-learning/english-grammar-advanced/coherence-and-